    "stac_version": "1.1.0",
    "description": "This derived product set consists of Global Navigation Satellite System Station Post-Seismic Deformation (PSD) model parameters available from the Crustal Dynamics Data Information System (CDDIS). The product provides the official, curated parametric models characterizing non-linear station motions following major earthquake events across the global tracking network of the International GNSS Service (IGS). Generated by the IGS Reference Frame Coordinator at the Institut National de l\u2019Information G\u00e9ographique et Foresti\u00e8re (IGN), this cumulative product defines earthquake epochs, functional decay types (logarithmic and exponential terms), relaxation amplitudes, and characteristic relaxation time constants across multi-year GNSS station coordinate time series.\nPost-seismic deformations result from transient solid-Earth processes following seismic ruptures\u2014including fault after slip, mantle viscoelastic relaxation, and crustal poroelastic rebound\u2014which cannot be accommodated by standard linear velocity formulations. Delivered in compressed Solution INdependent EXchange (SINEX) format, this product serves as an essential companion to cumulative IGS reference frame solutions (e.g., IGS20, IGb14) and the Discontinuities (DSC) product, enabling accurate non-linear trajectory modeling and unbiased coordinate and velocity determination across decades of space-geodetic observations.",
